      "problem": "Rationalize the denominator of $\\frac{4{c}^{2}-25}{\\sqrt{2c-1}+2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, note that the denominator's conjugate is $\\sqrt{2c-1}-2.$\n\nNow, to rationalize the denominator, we multiply both the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $\\sqrt{2c-1}-2,$ and simplify:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4{c}^{2}-25}{\\sqrt{2c-1}+2} & = \\\\ \\frac{4{c}^{2}-25}{\\sqrt{2c-1}+2}\\cdot \\frac{\\sqrt{2c-1}-2}{\\sqrt{2c-1}-2} & = \\\\ \\frac{(4{c}^{2}-25)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{(\\sqrt{2c-1}+2)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)} & = \\\\ \\frac{(4{c}^{2}-25)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{(\\sqrt{2c-1})^{2}-{2}^{2}} & = \\\\ \\frac{(2c+5)(2c-5)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{2c-1-4} & = \\\\ \\frac{(2c+5)(2c-5)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{2c-5} & = \\\\ \\frac{(2c+5)\\cancel{(2c-5)}(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)}{\\cancel{2c-5}} & = \\\\ (2c+5)(\\sqrt{2c-1}-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
